# Code ownership for review routing (CONTRIBUTING.md, governance).
#
# GitHub requests a review from the owner of every changed path. The security-
# and privacy-critical surfaces are listed explicitly so a change to the data
# contract, the workers, the URL serialization, the CSP or the supply-chain
# tooling always reaches a reviewer. Later lines win, so the specific rules
# below override the catch-all.

# Default owner for everything not matched more specifically.
*                               @chiaraberti13

# --- Security/privacy-critical core: text/byte contract, structured errors,
#     execution limits and cancellation. ---
/src/core/                      @chiaraberti13

# --- Heavy compute in workers (anti-ReDoS, timeouts, size limits). ---
/src/workers/                   @chiaraberti13

# --- Recipe serialization and migrations: URL safety, no secrets serialized. ---
/src/recipes/                   @chiaraberti13

# --- Content Security Policy and app entry points. ---
/index.html                     @chiaraberti13
/vercel.json                    @chiaraberti13
/vite.config.ts                 @chiaraberti13

# --- Supply chain: dependency manifest, lockfile and install hardening. ---
/package.json                   @chiaraberti13
/pnpm-lock.yaml                 @chiaraberti13
/.npmrc                         @chiaraberti13

# --- Release, CI and security policy. ---
/.github/                       @chiaraberti13
/SECURITY.md                    @chiaraberti13
